   "d": "2022-01-13",
   "doc": "Q1 TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Whilst both demand and returns rate uncertainty related to the Omicron variant are expected to remain in the short term, the guidance for the year remains unchanged with revenue growth expected in the range of 10%-15% and adjusted PBT of £110m-£140m",
   "file": "20220113_ASC_ASOS-Trading-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-04-12",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "Save for the removal of Russia's contribution to H2 following the decision to suspend sales announced on 2 March 2022, guidance remains unchanged although an increasingly challenging external environment introduces a greater degree of risk than normal",
   "file": "20220412_ASC_Interim-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-06-16",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -3,
   "q": "Guidance for the year updated to reflect uncertain consumer purchasing behaviour and the potential continuation of higher returns with revenue growth expected to be 4% to 7% and adjusted PBT now expected to be in the range of £20m to £60m",
   "file": "20220616_ASC_Trading-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-09-09",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "Profit is anticipated to be around the bottom end of company guidance, with constant currency sales growth of c.2% and net debt c. £150m",
   "file": "20220909_ASC_Trading-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-10-19",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "Against the backdrop of significant volatility in the macroeconomic environment, it is very difficult to predict consumer demand patterns for the upcoming year. Within the UK, ASOS expects a decline in the apparel market over the next 12 months but remains confident in its ability to take share against that backdrop.",
   "file": "20221019_ASC_Final-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-01-12",
   "doc": "Q1 TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "Revenue down 3%1, broadly in line with expectations, reflecting challenging trading conditions and prioritisation of structural profitability improvements and cash generation through a more disciplined approach to capital deployment.",
   "file": "20230112_ASC_Trading-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-05-10",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "For FY23, free cash outflow (prior to incremental refinancing costs) will be around £100m (i.e. around the bottom end of the £0 to £100m outflow guidance provided at FY22).",
   "file": "20230510_ASC_Interim-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-06-15",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Expectations for H2 FY23 and full-year FY23 are unchanged from guidance issued in the H1 FY23 results announcement on 10 May 2023, as updated on 25 May to account for the cash costs of re-financing.",
   "file": "20230615_ASC_Trading-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-09-26",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "EBIT is expected around the bottom of the guided £40m to £60m range, with free cash inflow in H2 now expected to be c.£60m excluding refinancing costs10 (previously £150m), principally as a result of timing effects that will reverse in September and October.",
   "file": "20230926_ASC_Trading-Statement.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-10-24",
   "doc": "OPS",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The performance for the period to 3 September 2023 is in-line with that reported at the post-close trading update on 26 September 2023, including",
   "file": "20231024_ASC_Notice-of-Full-Year-Results-and-Strategy-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-11-01",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "FY24 is about taking the necessary action to get us to that path. We expect the annualisation of Driving Change agenda profit initiatives to broadly mitigate the impacts of fixed cost deleverage from our expected revenue decline.",
